  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In 2025 remarks, Cassady said NTIA’s vision aligned with the Administration’s goal of U.S.-led AI powering the future and called AI-driven networks “table stakes” for future competitiveness (s2, s4). In April 2026 Senate testimony, he said AI, semiconductors, quantum, and related technologies will shape productivity, military power, and supply chains, and he advocated diplomacy that keeps the global digital economy open and builds coalitions of trusted partners (s1, s7). A State Department biography states that Cassady was appointed Ambassador at Large for Cyberspace and Digital Policy on August 7, 2026, and advances U.S. leadership abroad in AI and related critical and emerging technologies (s9).",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
    "s4",
    "s1",
    "s7",
    "s9"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In 2025 remarks, Cassady said NTIA’s vision aligned with the Administration’s goal of U.S.-led AI powering the future and called AI-driven networks “table stakes” for future competitiveness (s2, s4).",
